# GDI Full E2E → STAGED completion standard (permanent)

Applies to **all** GDI hotel research and publication work.

## Lifecycle

`FULL E2E → STAGED → FOUNDER APPROVAL → CURRENT`

## Binding statuses

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| RESEARCH IN PROGRESS | E2E incomplete |
| HOLD | More commercial evidence/qualification required |
| STAGED | Qualified, durably persisted, visible on `:8080` |
| CURRENT | Founder-approved customer publication |

Proposed Qualified / Write-Ready / QA Accepted are **internal only** — not founder gates. They auto-progress to STAGED when qualification + approved persistence + validation pass.

## Completion doctrine

Do **not** claim Full E2E COMPLETE because reports exist, unit FQO tests pass, or a proposed write-set was prepared.

COMPLETE requires: authorized research → commercial qualification → durable STAGED package → opportunity IDs reconciled → **visible in the integrated app on port 8080** → CURRENT unchanged unless explicitly approved for that exact `publicationVersion`.

## Must

- Reuse `Invoke-GdiFullE2E.ps1` / V3 orchestrator / publication package store (no parallel engines)
- Auto-stage complete qualified inventory after authorized E2E
- Preserve prior qualified IDs; Weekly Change for meaningful deltas
- Keep HOLD/rejected/speculative/incomplete out of qualified STAGED
- Never auto-publish CURRENT
- Preserve freezes, DryRun, and research budgets
- Validate on cumulative `:8080` (not isolated feature branch alone)

## Must not

- Add Proposed/HOLD founder inventory UIs or required URL params for review
- Fabricate opportunity counts
- Paid research / Findymail / auto-Surfe / CURRENT publish / schema changes / production deploy without separate founder authorization
- Independent merges from GDI chat

